cff-version: 1.2.0
title: WeavingSpace QGIS plugin
message: >-
  If you use this plugin in work you publish, please cite the article
  describing the technique (given under preferred-citation below). Cite
  the software itself as well if the implementation matters to your
  argument.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Luke
    family-names: Bergmann
    affiliation: University of British Columbia
repository-code: https://github.com/FoldingSpace/weavingspaceQGIS
url: https://foldingspace.github.io/weavingspaceQGIS/
abstract: >-
  A QGIS plugin for tiled and woven maps of multivariate area data. A
  repeating pattern of shapes is laid across a study area and each kind
  of shape carries a different attribute, so that several variables can
  be read from one map. The plugin builds on the weavingspace library
  by David O'Sullivan and Luke Bergmann, and returns ordinary QGIS
  layers seeded with standard renderers rather than a finished image.
  It is an experimental prototype.
keywords:
  - cartography
  - multivariate mapping
  - tiling
  - weaving
  - QGIS
  - choropleth
license: MIT
